  "sal_wins": "13/18 (magnitude-sliced rows omitted: identical to masked magnitude rows)",
  "environment_note": "A100-SXM4-80GB, torch 2.4.1+cu124, transformers 4.51.3, OMP_NUM_THREADS=12. facebook/dinov2-large (24 layers x 16 heads), seed 42, 5 epochs, SAL mask_ratio 0.3 (115/384 heads). Single seed.",
  "findings": [
    "DINOv2 is far more fragile to head removal than I-JEPA: 33% of heads already costs 6-54pp of linear probe depending on selection.",
    "Selection dominates: per-layer uniform random keeps 0.84 probe at 33% (sliced), global random 0.56, magnitude 0.36 (CKA 0.08). Magnitude selection is a poor baseline on DINOv2.",
    "SAL helps where the model survives: random-33% masked +9.8pp probe / +10.3pp kNN; random-uniform-33% sliced +3.0pp probe / +7.0pp kNN / +0.05 CKA. At 50% both arms collapse (probe 0.31-0.39) and gaps are mostly noise.",
    "SAL training loss rises (1.18 -> 2.44) while control falls (1.15 -> 0.64): with 30% of heads masked, DINOv2 does not recover the unmasked target within 5 epochs at lr 1e-5. Unpruned SAL-trained quality is unaffected (probe 0.8988 vs 0.8992).",
    "Head-set overlap between SAL training masks and post-hoc random selection is at chance level (simulated with the same seeds), so SAL's random-pruning gains are not from re-removing heads it trained without.",
    "Sliced: 304M -> 273M (33%) / 254M (50%); ~1.09-1.11x GPU, ~1.15-1.27x CPU; outputs identical to masked."
  ],
  "objective_note": "Same masked-prediction objective as I-JEPA runs; NOT DINOv2's self-distillation objective."
}